From b082747bdc7f9c6616dca59c58941cc233d0b6be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kush Jain <kush.jain@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 15:04:24 -0700
Subject: [EMBEDDEDSW PATCH] xilpm_ng: server: FPD Power-Cycle Handoff

Features:
- support for PowerUp Sequence of FPD Power Domain
- support for PowerDwn Sequence of FPD Power Domain
- support to request/release ACPU Core clocks
- support for PMC GIC Proxy (with RTC Alarm)
- support for Request WakeUp of Core0

Bug-fixes:
- bugfix to initialize OSPI clock in Init() drivers
- re-initialized the FPD Timestamp Counter on resume-path
- re-configured OSPI's operating mode to 1-1-1 before linux handoff

Workarounds:
- removed MMI devices from prealloc list of Default Subsystem
  Requirements
- added arbitrary 250ms delay after powering up FPD Rail

Note: This is not a complete production ready solution/patch; but rather
a crude engineered work to support complete FPD Power Cycle in Linux
suspend-resume feature.

Signed-off-by: Kush Jain <kush.jain@amd.com>

